## Bottom line

| Component | Started at server startup? | Scheduling |
|---|---|---|
| **`s3presign.Runner`** | **Yes** (`startBackgroundRunners`) | Immediate `RunOnce` + `time.Ticker` every 12h; per-object 4-day validity gate |
| **`memopayload.Runner`** | **No** (defined only) | N/A; `RebuildMemoPayload` runs synchronously on memo create/update |
| **`internal/scheduler`** | **No** (library + tests only) | Would use cron + `time.Timer`; never registered/started by server |
| **Store cache cleanup (×3)** | Yes, via `store.New` in `main` | `time.Ticker` every 5 min |
| **Webhook workers (×4)** | Yes, via `webhook` `init` | Channel queue (`asyncPostQueue`, cap 128) |
| **Email workers (×2)** | Yes, via `email` `init` | Channel queue (`asyncEmailQueue`, cap 128) |

The only item in `server/runner/` that the server **actually starts and schedules** is **`s3presign`**. The memo runner and the entire cron scheduler package are present in the repo but not hooked into server startup.

